# A range as a value (wiki/range.md): `a to b` (also `a … b`, `a through b`) the Range from a through b, `a upto b`
# (`a..b`) the same without b (lib/prelude.warp class Range). A loop over a range counts without one
# (extensions/sugar/iteration.warp). A rule, not an `infix operator` of the prelude: the rest of a list pattern,
# `rest...`, is the same operator with no end, which an operator's parameter cannot leave out
rewrite $a to $b => Range($a, $b, yes) where $a is not missing and $b is not missing
rewrite $a .. $b => Range($a, $b, no) where $a is not missing and $b is not missing

# A round group of items left as a value is the list of its items (decision immutable-tuple: round brackets are a plain
# list, card triage-round-groups): `(1, 2) == (3, 2)`, `([1, 2], [3, 4])[1][0]`, `f((1, 2))`. In the late sugar, after
# the lambdas and loops took their own groups (`(a, b) => …`, `for (k, v) in m`) and destructuring its (tuples.warp)
rewrite ($a, $b, $rest...) => [$a, $b, $rest...]
